> I don't often poly into nymphs or leprechauns, so I'm not sure - does
> playing as them have unexpected results as it stands?

A player polymorphed into a nymph or leprechaun will enjoy the
monster's special attack when meleeing things, namely you'll be able
to steal monster inventory or gold, respectively. 

Of course, stealing gold is practically worthless apart from milking
priests for protection (still requires a way to re-pacify the cleric).
Being able to rob monsters blind can, however, be enormously useful -
steal a monster's wand of death, amulet of life saving, potion of full
healing etc. Time and again, you'll steal a captain's plate mail or
the like, though ...

